        "reading": "Integrated advanced legal examination. First identify the parties, forum, operative date and controlling legal authority. Create an issue tree with each required element, mark disputed and missing facts, and determine which side bears the burden. Draft a position for each side before selecting a reasoned outcome. Different doctrines require separate analyses even when a narrative connects them. Do not rely on the multiple-choice result as a grade for independent writing. Source citations must be verified against primary documents and later controlling developments.\n\nCase-specific analytical method: Begin with the actual scenario: A director owns 15% of a supplier acquired by the corporation. Minutes show the director participated in pricing negotiations but abstained from the final vote. Do not assume that the allegations are proven. List each actor, disputed fact, required evidentiary foundation, and burden of proof. Evaluate the strongest response: Directors argue independent approval on informed advice; shareholders claim concealment and an unfair price. Identify the exact proposition supported by Applicable state corporate law and governing entity statute, check whether that authority controls in the selected jurisdiction, and distinguish any conflicting or later decisions. Write a provisional conclusion conditioned on facts that remain unknown. Then change one material fact and explain whether the legal outcome would change. This exercise develops legal reasoning; neither a keyword match nor a quiz establishes mastery.",
