        "reading": "Determine capitalized cost, placed-in-service date, asset classification, applicable recovery system, convention and potential expensing elections. Separate financial statement treatment from federal tax recovery and identify tax-year limits. Avoid inserting unverified current-year rates or assuming bonus depreciation applies universally. Worked analysis sequence: specify jurisdiction and time, identify the contested element and its burden, list facts supporting and undermining each position, then state a conditional conclusion. Explain how a change in one fact would alter the result. Primary law must be independently checked for currency, subsequent treatment and applicability.\n\nCase-specific analytical method: Begin with the actual scenario: A company installs equipment halfway through a tax year and incorrectly expenses the entire cost without documenting any election. Do not assume that the allegations are proven. List each actor, disputed fact, required evidentiary foundation, and burden of proof. Evaluate the strongest response: Taxpayer asserts immediate deduction; examiner challenges eligibility and useful classification. Identify the exact proposition supported by Internal Revenue Code §§167, 168 and relevant tax-year rules, check whether that authority controls in the selected jurisdiction, and distinguish any conflicting or later decisions. Write a provisional conclusion conditioned on facts that remain unknown. Then change one material fact and explain whether the legal outcome would change. This exercise develops legal reasoning; neither a keyword match nor a quiz establishes mastery.",
